<div class="alert alert-info">For location columns, <a href="<?= e(url('locations')) ?>">add your locations first</a> and use their exact names in the CSV. Alternatively, use <code>polling_station_code</code> for the official polling station ID; its region, constituency and branch are derived automatically. Supplied location names must agree with that ID. Keep IDs as text to preserve leading zeros. Without an official ID, a constituency requires its region; a polling station or branch requires its constituency. A polling station does not require a branch. Unknown or inconsistent locations are marked as problems in the preview. Nothing is saved until you confirm.</div><section class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body"><form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" action="<?= e(url('imports')) ?>"><?= csrf() ?><input type="hidden" name="_action" value="voters_upload"><?= input('file','Voter list CSV','','file',true,'accept=".csv,text/csv"') ?><p class="form-text">Required columns: <code>voter_id</code>, <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code>. Legacy <code>full_name</code> or <code>given_names</code> plus <code>surname</code> is also accepted. Every row being added or updated must include <code>polling_station_code</code>, or an exact <code>polling_station</code> name with its <code>constituency</code> and <code>region</code>. Missing or unknown stations are preview issues and cannot be imported. Other template columns are optional. Residential address columns are <code>address</code>, <code>town</code>, <code>residential_district</code> and <code>residential_region</code>; these are separate from electoral location columns. Use UTF-8 CSV; dates use YYYY-MM-DD. Up to 10 MB / 20,000 voters.</p><label class="form-check mb-3"><input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="update_existing" value="1"><span class="form-check-label">Update existing non-member voters when the voter ID matches.</span></label><p class="small text-secondary">Without this option, existing voter IDs are skipped. Blank optional cells never erase existing details during an update. Existing members are always skipped, including inactive members. Update their personal and membership details through their member profile. Member skips are included in the Skipped total. This step only prepares a preview; it does not change voter records.</p><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Preview voter upload</button> <a class="btn btn-light" href="<?= e(url('voters')) ?>">View voters</a></form></div></section>
<section class="card"><div class="card-header"><h2 class="card-title">Recent uploads</h2></div><?php if(!$imports): ?><div class="card-body"><p class="mb-0">No uploads yet. The template contains headers only.</p></div><?php else: ?><div class="table-responsive"><table class="table align-middle"><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Added</th><th>Updated</th><th>Skipped</th><th>Uploaded by</th><th>Date</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($imports as $upload): ?><tr><td><?= e($upload['filename']) ?></td><td><?= number($upload['added_count']) ?></td><td><?= number($upload['updated_count']) ?></td><td><?= number($upload['skipped_count']) ?></td><td><?= e($upload['imported_by']) ?></td><td><?= date_display($upload['created_at'],true) ?></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?></tbody></table></div><?php endif; ?></section>
